 ## The memory model
 
+- **Allocation pressure.** Pool growth is bounded by the advertised GPU heaps (at most one
+  sixteenth of the smallest usable heap and 64 MiB). If growth fails, idle blocks on that heap
+  are released and the resource can take an exact-size dedicated block. Host imports also release
+  idle blocks on their heap before a bounded retry. Live resources keep their memory; a required
+  allocation that still fails reports the real error. Bounded pressure records distinguish the
+  resource's size from speculative growth and report retained allocator bytes.
